WEBVTT

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.820
Have the servants handle the rest.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:49.790
Oh.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.970
You've come to see me, Richard.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.680
York of the white rose.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.220
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:08.770
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.400
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.620
Your Majesty!

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.580
Are you awake?!

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:56.550
You must be tired. It's been so long since
you last attended to public business.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.640
Your Majesty, how do you feel?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.300
Warwick.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:09.430
God's will and your hand have
freed me from my imprisonment.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:13.440
But this place...
This place is suffocating.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.190
Why not depart the palace for a time?

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.440
What?

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.490
I mean rest your mind on a pilgrimage.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:26.280
That should be the best thing
for your health as well.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.500
But if I did that...

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:34.210
Have no fear. We shall bear
the heavy burden of government.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:39.800
You needn't appear in public; we'll let
it be known that you've taken ill.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.470
I suppose you're right.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.720
This must be a sign from God.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.270
Warwick, I name you Protector.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.440
I relinquish my authority to you.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.900
A wise decision, Your Majesty.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.740
Margaret is still in France.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.570
If we can assault London now--

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:10.410
It's a shame about Anne.
Weren't you fond of each other?

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:14.170
And that Lancastrian brat,
of all people, took her from you.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.040
If that's how it appeared to you,

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.880
it was a trick of Warwick's machinations.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:25.720
He's a crafty man. Crafty enough
to inveigle my own brother.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.930
Warwick and George are the
greatest nobles save the king.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.560
Anthony and Hastings have returned to us,

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.650
but our forces are still insufficient.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:41.110
Therefore, I'd like to ask a favor of you.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.030
While I admire His Majesty's
wisdom and virtue,

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.660
I must object to his choice
of officers for once.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:50.830
Why, my lord?

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.920
Because there is someone far more
fit to be Protector than me.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.250
Duke George.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:04.380
This is our sovereign's will,
but how will you take it?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.760
I...

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:12.680
Ever since I betrayed my brother,
I've had no choice but to trust this man.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:18.020
If you agree to it, then so will I.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.770
But first, I want to discuss
the succession to--

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:24.110
Our first order of business is
to declare Edward a traitor.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:27.910
We must confiscate all his
wealth and lands at once.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:28.910
Of course, but--

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:31.410
We'll discuss that at another time.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.620
George and the Lancastrian prince.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:40.880
Whichever I eventually
place on the throne,

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.960
the choice is mine to make.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.720
I have everything in hand.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:51.810
I am now the King of England
in all but name.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.610
Catesby, take this.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:08.740
Richard, deliver this
Yorkist flag to George.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:12.240
Tell him that this is my final warning,

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.500
and that he's free to
choose how he uses it.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.630
Handle it carefully, and don't
let anyone see inside it.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:28.170
Must Your Grace carry out such
a dangerous mission yourself?

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.930
The fact that he entrusted it to me

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.970
means that I'm to do all
I can to convince George.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:39.350
I see. I'm in awe of the strength
of your brotherly bonds.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:44.480
This is less "brotherly love"
than it is a battle for pride.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.820
If we lose, there will be
no victory in the real war.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.070
Not for any of us.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:53.030
Your Grace.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:58.160
But the bond between George
and Warwick is surprisingly firm.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:04.380
George stayed with Warwick even after he
sided with Lancaster. Can I move him?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.250
Can I...?

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.170
No. I <i>will </i>succeed.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:12.010
I'll win England back from them.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.100
Hey. You there.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.390
They're in a carriage. Outrun them.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.490
Well?

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.370
Nothing unusual.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:39.200
But I hear that group from
earlier is at a nearby inn.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.370
We'll lodge here for the night.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:44.750
Investigate them just
in case, and be careful.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.210
This is holy ground.

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.510
Your Majesty.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.930
Remove your weapons and join me in prayer.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:59.600
No matter where I run,
death and bloodshed follow me.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.020
Your Majesty, you mustn't
listen to his honeyed words.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.770
He schemes to bend
Your Majesty to his will.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.650
--It's treachery.
--It's treason, Your Majesty.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:08.940
--Command us.
--Order us.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.190
--Your Majesty.
--Your Majesty!

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.440
Your Majesty!

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:18.160
Please, take me somewhere far away,

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.160
to a truly free world,
kind and filled with love.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:25.500
Richard.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.670
Another infiltration, then?

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:35.260
That was a crisis,
and we had a collaborator.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:38.430
Even if we do, we'll need more--

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:41.560
Your meals are ready, my good sirs.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:42.890
Did you order food?

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:46.980
I serve all my guests a light meal.
You have the place to yourselves today!

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.070
Now please, come downstairs.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.210
Hey.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:07.420
We've changed our minds.
Bring our meals to this room.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.750
Yes, sir. Right away.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:14.800
Honestly. We can't even
eat in peace like this.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.180
Shall we change inns?

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:18.470
No.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:20.850
I'm sure of it.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:24.140
So, that group we saw
<i>were </i>Yorkist remnants.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.690
That flag you say you saw proves it.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.360
Outside!

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.360
I'll follow you!

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.110
Wait!

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:38.200
Yorkist dregs!
Have you come for his life?!

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.370
Who?

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.120
I won't let you!

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:51.210
A Lancastrian noble?
He seemed like a man of some status.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.750
What is he doing here?

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.430
Henry?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:09:59.970
Richard.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.100
Where did he go?!

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.770
Find him!

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:04.680
Come on!

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.440
Richard...

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.230
Richard!

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.190
What are you doing here?

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.440
Richard, you're hurt!

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.530
This isn't...

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.490
...my blood...

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.540
Richard!

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:28.160
Mr. Catesby, sir!

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.420
Explanations can wait. Let's go.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.960
Edward.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.050
You took this lovely maiden's hand

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:41.800
and made a firm vow to make
her your wife, did you not?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.970
Yes, Mother. I gladly made her my wife.

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:51.190
If that's so, why haven't you
consummated your marriage yet?

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.150
W-Well...

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:56.440
There are any number of ways
to put someone in the mood.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.190
M-Mother.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:04.080
Do it tonight. Is that clear?

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.620
Do your duty. Love is not necessary.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.100
I know everything.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:31.140
You... had feelings
for Richard, didn't you?

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:34.190
I did.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.480
This isn't only hard on you, you know!

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:38.940
I was in love with a woman myself!

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:41.030
If your feelings still persist, then--

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:44.870
No. I've already rid myself of them.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.040
Is that all?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:50.120
Was your love so easily discarded?

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.500
Unbelievable.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.500
My feelings are nothing like yours.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:01.550
I swore an oath to God
that I would have her.

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:04.090
That I'd let nothing stop me.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.140
--Not even--
--You have no idea!

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:10.770
You can't imagine how deeply
I cared for Duke Richard!

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.940
Your feelings don't amount
to much! I can tell!

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:16.400
--You couldn't!
--I do!

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:20.150
I love Richard far more than you do!

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.360
God...

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.660
...would never allow such a thing.
I mean--

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.290
It's your love He won't allow.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.830
If you still have regrets, I'll tell you:

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.870
Richard...

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.590
...is actually a woman.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:43.380
She normally dresses as a man
and lives hiding her true sex.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.050
Please be serious.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:47.350
It's a lie.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:52.140
I know that Duke Richard is as
slender and pretty as a woman, but...

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:53.770
Still,

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.230
he did always seem to be
hiding something deep in his heart.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:02.070
Got that? No matter how
deeply you love Richard,

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:07.490
as long as you're a woman,
she'll never requite your feelings.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.420
Are you all right, Richard?

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.460
Henry.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:25.630
Are there any yarrow leaves near here?

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:28.600
They're jagged leaves on a tall plant.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.560
I understand. Wait for me!

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:39.690
It will take a deeper
wound than this to kill me.

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.530
I need to rejoin Catesby
and the others soon.

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:47.910
Richard, are you at death's door?

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.490
Die!

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:53.660
Vanish alone, deep in the forest.

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:56.160
No one will save you.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:00.000
No one will mourn a demon's death.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.380
In the end, you're all alone.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.220
Until the very end!

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.020
Richard.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:20.310
We've come to punish you.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:22.610
To punish you for surviving.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:24.900
To punish you for being born.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.570
Back then...

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:30.780
You should have died!

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.210
Begone, demon!

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:38.120
Henry.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:43.040
O Lord, protect him.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:47.760
If you must take a life,
at least make it mine.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:58.770
Could you see the demons?

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:04.400
Wolves are demons given flesh.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:06.990
The Lord God saved us.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:13.030
I thought... I thought that I
would never see you again.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.830
I thought I <i>shouldn't </i>see you again.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.080
And yet...

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:23.880
I've missed you all this time.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:26.170
I longed to see you, Richard.

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:29.130
I'm truly, truly glad.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.260
Duke Richard.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:39.480
No animals will come here.
I found it earlier.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.560
Aren't you cold?

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.820
Henry... You're warm.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.960
It wasn't a dream.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.300
Richard. I'm so glad.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.600
It wasn't a dream.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:19.890
I'm sorry! Your wound...

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:22.770
I'll pick fresh leaves for you.

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:23.810
Wait.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.900
Richard?

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:27.900
It's nothing.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.280
Why am I so fainthearted?

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.740
I'll be right back.

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:36.120
I can't afford to die.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.540
Not until England belongs
to the House of York again.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:48.250
But if I fail to convince George,
I might be killed on the spot.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.090
Hurry back, Henry.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.970
So, they did flee on horseback.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.640
Do you think the king is safe?

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:04.940
The king? Henry should be in the Tower
of London. What would bring him here?

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.860
But Duke Richard matters more now.

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:12.490
Richard!

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:16.490
If it hurts, drink this.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:20.080
I found a spring, but I had
nothing to carry water in.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.200
This is fine.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.370
Stay here. I'll leave as soon as I'm well.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:35.010
When I look up at the sky,
I remember the first time I met you.

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:39.140
You never change, do you?

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:43.810
I often dream of my mother abandoning me.

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.390
Do you still have nightmares?

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:50.520
The world stays just the same,

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:56.110
but my beautiful memories
with you purify me.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.530
They beautify the world.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:07.830
Even alone, it wasn't frightening.

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:14.010
Rather... the loneliness has been
kind ever since losing Father.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.430
That's why I swore to never waver again.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:19.840
And yet...

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:26.390
You weaken me.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:32.570
Should you be moving?

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:35.900
I'll starve if I leave everything to you.

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:37.490
You mentioned a spring?

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.570
Yes. I marked a trail there.

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:44.580
Well done. I'll fetch water today.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.870
You'll go alone?

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.290
Gather branches and wait for me.

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:57.130
So many signs. Is he a child?

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.010
No one will see me here.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:17.070
Should you be in the water?

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.990
I'm fine! I'm just washing out the blood.

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:22.370
What if you collapsed? I'll help you.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.490
Stay back.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.790
If you come near me now...

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:34.630
...you'll see this body of mine.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.130
Richard.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:40.470
You're bloodstained.

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:45.470
You're all clean now, Richard.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.270
You're truly... spotless.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.360
Oh, my.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:57.530
What a surprise. Someone beat us here.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:59.490
I'll get out first, Henry.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:03.450
I haven't seen you around.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.030
Village girls? I'm in luck.

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.080
If I dress now, then...

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:12.750
Oh, my. What a lovely
face you've got, mister.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:17.670
This is our secret paradise.

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:20.840
Tell you what. For you,

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:22.800
I'll make it free.

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:26.640
What?!

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.260
Hey! Henry!

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:34.690
Mother. Mother.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.900
Mother?

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:41.490
How wicked of you.
Henry can see us, you know.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:45.160
It's fine. He's still a child.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:48.030
You're the only one I truly love.

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:53.120
Let's leave all the rest to Henry and
spend every day together like this.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:57.090
You're a demon. The loveliest
and most lascivious there is.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.920
You're right; I am a demon.

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.460
A demon of love.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:10.060
My mother's infidelity and betrayal
never stopped haunting me.

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.310
It was like a curse.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.730
And that's why you fear them?

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:17.270
You see women as demons?

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:21.320
No. It's not women that I fear.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.240
What frightens me is...

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:26.200
...desire.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.990
Love--lust--is a sin.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.000
I'm in pain, but why?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.540
I won't love anyone.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:38.000
Why does it hurt?

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:43.340
I don't need anyone to love if I have
a friend I can trust with all my heart.

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:46.890
I'm not a woman, and yet...

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:52.770
You're my angel, Richard.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:59.980
I love Henry.
